  "issues": [
    "The commands to manage the NVIDIA MPS daemon (`nvidia-cuda-mps-control -d` and `echo quit | nvidia-cuda-mps-control`) are executed without a parallel launcher like `flux run`. In a multi-node job, this means the daemon will only be started and stopped on the single node where the main batch script executes (the lead node). The MPI tasks that land on the second node will not have an MPS daemon to connect to, which will likely cause them to fail or fall back to non-MPS execution, impacting performance. These commands should be wrapped in `flux run` to ensure they execute on all allocated nodes."
  ]
}
